{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793641941,"nonce":"gNPPmnELw0QgI1aPZKRDOHXTp4A=","title":"Interpreter recompiles a function's bytecode on nested or recursive calls","message":"hir_interp.rs call_by_id removes the CompiledFunction from self.cache for the whole frame and re-inserts it afterwards. A nested call to the same function finds no entry and recompiles its bytecode (compile_function_with, SipHash, hashbrown inserts, malloc/free, body_source locks). Every call also pays a hash remove and insert of a struct with about twenty Vec fields.\n\nRepro: ZYNTAX_BASELINE_THRESHOLD=1000000000 zypy run fib.py with fib(22): 57,313 calls, 150 ms, about 2.6 us per call. Applies to any recursive or mutually recursive function while it waits for its baseline compile, and permanently to functions that stay interpreted (TS interpreter profile).\n\nDirection: keep Rc/Arc\u003cCompiledFunction\u003e in the cache and clone the handle; no remove/insert.","files":null}]}